ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559564 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "df0cddb8-e92c-55c7-aa50-0c028229c858" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559604 #edb/ref 1080 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-4,\\,b=⟨1,1,-1⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559604 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559604 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f182158c-1a39-52d9-93a0-587908c41e2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559616 #edb/ref 1080 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-2,\\,b=⟨6,2,-5⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559616 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559616 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f462a311-ea89-555c-9281-1e9601a16c66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559623 #edb/ref 1080 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨6,-2,-5⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559623 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559623 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f66ecaf3-9ca2-57cf-a1ac-6666ad1e34d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186559042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559660 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2364b0d7-2e01-5066-ae19-026ea99bfd99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186559616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559691 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "55c226f4-65ae-55eb-8831-38644f8ba978" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186559341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559741 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b9c0353c-be95-5a9c-955e-2c015a02fd36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559772 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559772 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71392" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559772 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559772 #edb/ref 1071 "The intersection of the planes $-x+z-1=0$ and $y+z+5=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559772 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0174198f-a0ad-5395-9af8-f36d4c14897b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559772 #edb/ref 1074 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this to the first equation gives\n\n$$\n-x+0-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=-1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\ny+0+5=0\\,⟹\\,y=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=⟨-1,-5,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $-x+z-1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-1,0,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $y+z+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-1,-5,0⟩+t⟨-1,1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-1+(-5)=-6,$ and $b=⟨-1,1,-1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559877 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559877 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71467" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559877 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559877 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the two planes $3x-6y+1=0$ and $-x+2y=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n\nII. The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nIII. The planes intersect in a straight line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559877 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8cdac5c-1e47-510f-8a9c-c4df54b69f10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559877 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that:  \n\n- For the plane $3x-6y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,-6,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $-x+2y=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨-1,2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,-6,0⟩\\times ⟨-1,2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =0i+0j+0k \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}=0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are parallel. However,  the second plane passes through the origin  $O(0,0,0)$ but the first plane doesn't: \n\n$$\n3(0)-6(0)+1=1\\ne 0\n$$\n\n So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since planes are parallel but not coincident, they cannot intersect.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559889 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559889 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71414" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559889 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559889 #edb/ref 1071 "The intersection of the planes $x+2y+2z=0$ and $4x-2y+4z+8=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559889 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fad299b6-2750-5729-9622-52ccf21ff85a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559889 #edb/ref 1074 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives \n\n$$\nx+2(0)+2z=0\\,⟹\\,x=-2z,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ and $x=-2z$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+4z+8 & =0 \\\\ 4(-2z)-2(0)+4z+8 & =0 \\\\ -4z & =-8 \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-2z=-4$ and $a=⟨-4,0,2⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+2y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,2,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $4x-2y+4z+8=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨4,-2,4⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,2,2⟩\\times ⟨4,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =12i+4j-10k \\\\  & =⟨12,4,-10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n\n$$\nb=\\frac{1}{2}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨6,2,-5⟩.\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-4,0,2⟩+t⟨6,2,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-4+2=-2,$ and $b=⟨6,2,-5⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
